  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry, tranquil and milder weather extends right \nthrough Saturday\n\n850 mb ridge axis still to our west over eastern Ohio and the\n\"Rule of Thumb\" here on the downwind side of Lake Erie is to \nhold onto the bulk of clouds across the upslope areas until the \nridge axis drifts overhead and to the east.\n\nThat being said, the extensive shallow stratocu across the\nNorthern and Western Mtns of PA this evening will continue to\nhold tough for the next 5-8 hours before the mean/shallow\nboundary layer flow backs about 20-30 deg (to the west) after\nmidnight.  \n\nThe sky cover will be a big factor for minimum temps with \n25-35F spread. Less confident in fog potential given cloud \ntrends, but after 08Z there could be 2-4 hours of patchy fog\nwith temps slipping into the low 30s. Widespread sunshine still\nexpected by Tuesday afternoon.\n\nA string of sunny and increasingly warmer days followed by\nmainly clear and chilly nights is ahead for the remainder of \nthe week into the weekend. Fcst Max temps peak 10-20 degrees \nabove the historical average Thu-Sun while nights will run \ncloser to climo resulting in large diurnal ranges indicative of \na prolonged late Autumn dry spell. Expect ideal conditions for \noutdoor pre-winter activities: raking leaves, set up holiday \ndecorations, or enjoying time outside, it will be an very \npleasant stretch of weather for the 3rd week of November. \n\nWith the resumption of another prolonged dry stretch, fire \nweather concerns could increase as we get later into November \nand December. Any particularly windy patterns with minimal \nprecipitation could lead to an elevated risk of rapid wildfire \nspread.",
